# [[ .Name ]]

A [tug](https://github.com/cuonggt/tug) app: Go handlers render [[ .Framework ]] pages
through Inertia, with no API in between.

```sh
[[ if or .SQLite (not .Database) -]]
tug dev      # run it on http://localhost:8080, rebuilt and reloaded as it changes
tug gen      # write the TypeScript of the pages' props and the routes
tug build    # build it into one binary, frontend included
go test ./...
[[- else -]]
docker compose up -d   # start the database, which tug dev and the tests use
tug dev                # run it on http://localhost:8080, rebuilt and reloaded as it changes
tug gen                # write the TypeScript of the pages' props and the routes
tug build              # build it into one binary, frontend included
go test ./...
[[- end ]]
```

- `main.go`: the server, its pages and routes, and the health check at
  `/up`. A page is declared with `tug.Page[Props]("Name")`, and its
  component is `resources/js/pages/Name.[[ .Component ]]`. Its pages run
  the scripts that carry their nonce alone, by a Content-Security-Policy,
  as `app.html`'s do: what it blocks, the log says.
[[- if .Database ]]
- `database.go`: the app's database, which `db.go` opens,
[[- if .SQLite ]] SQLite
  (`app.db`, or `DB_PATH`),
[[- else ]] [[ .DatabaseName ]] at
  `DB_URL`, which `compose.yaml` runs in development, and the tests make
  a database each on,
[[- end ]] through `database/sql`, and what tug's packages
  keep in it, a table each, with its SQL in a `_db.go` file: the
  background jobs, `jobs.go`, which run beside the server, `QUEUE_WORKERS`
  at once, a job that fails running again later; the cache, which the
  starter keeps nothing in yet; the sessions, which
  `SESSION_STORE=database` keeps there rather than in their cookies; the
  throttles' counts; and the events the hub carries to the pages open on
  every instance of the app. A handler's writes go in one transaction,
  with the jobs and the events about them, by `data.inTx`.
- `migrations/`: the migrations that make and change the tables, a file of
  SQL each, named for when it was made, which run once, in order, as the
  app starts: `migrations.go`. `tug migrate new create_posts` writes the
  next, and `./[[ .Name ]] migrate status` lists them.
[[- if .SQLite ]]
- `backup.go`: the database's backups, which a copy of `app.db` made as
  the app writes can't be: `./[[ .Name ]] backup <file>` makes one while it
  serves, and every night the `backup-db` job puts one on the app's disk,
  in `files/backups/`, or with `FILESYSTEM_DISK=s3` in a bucket, off the
  machine, keeping the newest `BACKUP_KEEP`, 7 unless it says.
[[- end ]]
[[- end ]]
- `resources/js/app.[[ .Script ]]`: the app in the browser, which `inertia.[[ .Script ]]`
[[- if .SSR ]]
  makes, and `ssr.[[ .Script ]]`, the app on the server. A first visit's page
  renders there first, with Node, which the app runs beside it from the
  SSR build in `ssr/build`; under tug dev, Vite renders it.
[[- else ]]
  makes.
[[- end ]]
- `lang/`: the app's languages, a file each, as `tug lang vi` writes
  `lang/vi.json` with every text the app and its pages say, to translate.
  The binary embeds them, and `APP_LOCALE` is the one a browser gets that
  asks for none of them. A page says its own words with `useLang`, from
  `resources/js/lib/lang.ts`, as the home page does, and a number and a
  time the language's way with its `n()` and `d()`.
- `resources/js/tug`: the TypeScript tug gen writes from the Go types. It
  isn't edited by hand; tug dev and tug build write it again.
- `AGENTS.md`: how to change the app, for a coding agent, its rules, the
  commands that check a change, and how to see it running, which
  `CLAUDE.md` hands Claude Code.
- `tug.json`: the tug whose starter the app has, and the flags it was made
  with, which `tug upgrade` reads to bring the app what the starter has
  gained since, merged into its own changes.
- `.env`: read by tug dev. `APP_KEY` encrypts the sessions, and a deployed
  app needs one of its own, set in its environment, with `APP_URL`, its
  own address, and `TRUSTED_PROXIES` behind a load balancer; or, on a
  machine of its own, `TLS_DOMAINS`, for the app to serve HTTPS itself,
  with certificates from Let's Encrypt.
[[- if .Postgres ]] Its database is `DB_URL`, which
  is compose.yaml's in development.
[[- else if .MySQL ]] Its database is `DB_URL`, which is
  compose.yaml's in development.
[[- end ]]
[[- if .Database ]] `tug run` runs the binary's commands
  with it, as `tug run migrate status`.
[[- end ]]
[[ if .SSR -]]
- `Dockerfile`: the app as one static binary on a distroless image with
[[- if .SQLite ]]
  Node, for the pages it renders on the server, and the database, its
  backups and the certificates of `TLS_DOMAINS` on a volume.
[[- else ]]
  Node, for the pages it renders on the server, and the certificates of
  `TLS_DOMAINS` on a volume.
[[- end ]]
[[- else -]]
- `Dockerfile`: the app as one static binary on a distroless image, with
[[- if .SQLite ]]
  the database, its backups and the certificates of `TLS_DOMAINS` on a
  volume.
[[- else ]]
  the certificates of `TLS_DOMAINS` on a volume.
[[- end ]]
[[- end ]]
